WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.961 --> 00:00:08.466
[Violinist plays Paganini
“Caprice No. 17”]

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:17.934
One of the things that's
so wonderful about the violin is

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.519
it is a very difficult
instrument,

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.521
which means
you can never be too relaxed

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:25.024
♪

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:26.109
and you always have

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:28.695
to push yourself to be better
every single day.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.947
♪

00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:34.576
My name is Ilana Zaks,
and I'm a violinist

00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:36.202
at the Yale School of Music

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.079
studying in the Master
of Musical Arts program.

00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:40.498
♪

00:00:45.962 --> 00:00:49.966 line:76%
How can you present
an experience that is accessible

00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:52.260 line:71%
to as many people as possible?

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.723 align:start position:0% line:68%
So I really wanted to bring
history, accessibility, music,

00:00:56.723 --> 00:00:58.433
into one space

00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:01.519
and to bring it specifically
to Sprague Memorial Hall.

00:01:02.187 --> 00:01:05.398
In classical music,
the stage is a little bit

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.902
more of a rigid space,
which is why for my recital,

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:12.030
I really wanted to find a way
of bringing

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:17.535
this environment of community
and intimacy into one space.

00:01:18.036 --> 00:01:20.413
I really wanted to experiment
with technology,

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:24.125
and I wanted to experiment
with storytelling and in a way

00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:28.087
the whole recital is
one big story about history.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.340
♪

00:01:33.134 --> 00:01:36.679
You will probably never be able
to recreate that performance,

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:39.682
exactly,
after that moment is done.

00:01:39.682 --> 00:01:41.935
♪

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:46.356
What I hope to accomplish in
this performance is

00:01:46.356 --> 00:01:49.651
to bring everything
that I've learned here at Yale

00:01:49.692 --> 00:01:51.069
into one performance

00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:54.823
and to present it to everyone
as a gift from my heart

00:01:54.823 --> 00:01:57.367
to the community that
has made my life so special.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:02:01.746
♪♪

